hadiths[23]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2927","# Translation of the Hadith\n\n**Ishaaq ibn Mansoor narrated to us:** Abdur-Razzaaq informed us: Ja'far ibn Sulaymaan narrated to us: Thaabit narrated to us from Anas رضي الله عنه that the Prophet ﷺ entered Makkah during the compensatory 'Umrah (i.e., 'Umrah al-Qadaa'), and 'Abdullaah ibn Rawaahah رضي الله عنه was walking before him, reciting:\n\n*\Make way"," O sons of the disbelievers"," from his path!*\n*Today we shall strike you concerning its revelation","*\n*A strike that shall sever the heads from their resting places","*\n*And shall render the companion oblivious of his companion.\""*\n\nThereupon 'Umar رضي الله عنه said: \""O Ibn Rawaahah! In the presence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and within the Sacred Precinct of Allah"," you recite poetry?\"" The Prophet ﷺ said: **\""Leave him"," O 'Umar"," for it is swifter upon them than the flight of arrows.\""**\n\nAbu 'Eesaa (at-Tirmidhee) said: **\""This is a hasan saheeh ghareeb hadith from this chain.\""**\n\nAbdur-Razzaaq also narrated this hadith from Ma'mar"," from az-Zuhree"," from Anas"," in a similar manner. It has also been narrated in other narrations that the Prophet ﷺ entered Makkah during 'Umrah al-Qadaa' with **Ka'b ibn Maalik** رضي الله عنه walking before him. This is considered more correct by some scholars of hadith"," because 'Abdullaah ibn Rawaahah رضي الله"""
"2928","Narrated Anas bin Malik:\The Prophet (ﷺ) would recite: 'Anin-nafsu Bin-Nafsi Wal-'Ainu Bil-'Aini'\"" (From 5:)"""
"2929","Narrated Mu'adh bin Jabal:\The Prophet (ﷺ) would recite: 'Hal Tastati'u Rabbak"""
"2930","Narrated Umm Salamah:\The Prophet (ﷺ) would recite: 'Innahu 'Amila Ghaira Salih"""
"2931","Narrated Umm Salamah:\The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) recited this Ayah: 'Innahu 'Amalun Ghairu Salih'\"" (11:)"""
"2932","Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us: Yahya ibn Sa'id informed us, from Shu'bah, from Qatadah, from Yunus ibn Jubayr, from Muhammad ibn Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \That the belly of one of you be filled with pus is better for him than that it be filled with poetry.\"" He said: This is a hasan sahih hadith."""
"2933","Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:from Ubay bin Ka'b that the Prophet (ﷺ) recited: \Fi 'Ainin Hami'ah\"" (18:)"""
"2934","Narrated to us Isḥāq ibn Mūsā al-Anṣārī, 'Abdullāh ibn Wahb related to us, from 'Abd al-Jabbār ibn 'Umar, from Muḥammad ibn al-Munkadar, from Jābir, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, forbade a man from sleeping on a rooftop that is not walled around.\n\nAbū 'Īsā [al-Tirmidhī] said: This is a gharīb (uncommon) hadith. We do not know it as a narration from Muḥammad ibn al-Munkadar from Jābir except through this chain. And 'Abd al-Jabbār ibn 'Umar al-Aylī is considered weak (yuḍa''af)."
"2935","Narrated Ibn 'Umar:that he recited the following to the Prophet (ﷺ): \Who created you in the weakness (Min Da'f)\"" So he said: \""Min Du'f\"" (Another chain) with similar in meaning"""
"2936","Narrated 'Abdullah bin Mas'ud:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) would recite: \Then is there anyone who would remember? (54:)"""
"2937","Narrated 'Aishah:that the Prophet (ﷺ) would recite: \Furuhun Wa Raihanun Wa Jannatu Na'im (56:)"""
"2938","Narrated 'Alqamah:\We arrived in Ash-Sham and we went to Abu Ad-Darda. So he said: 'Is there any among you who can recite for me according to the recitation of 'Abdullah?'\"" He said: \""They pointed to me"""
"2939","Narrated 'Abdullah:\The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) recited to me: \""Indeed Allah is the Provider"""
"2940","Qutaybah narrated to us, who said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said:\n\n\When you travel through fertile land"," give the camels their share of the earth (i.e."," let them graze). When you travel during a year of drought"," hasten to preserve their marrow (i.e."," spare them from hardship). And when you camp for the night"," avoid the road"," for it is the path of beasts and the dwelling of harmful creatures at night.\""\n\nHe (the narrator) said: This is a hasan sahih hadith. There are narrations on this topic from Jabir and Anas"," may Allah be pleased with them."""
"2941","Narrated 'Abdullah:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \How horrible it is for one of them - or - one of you to say: \""I have forgotten such and such Ayah"""
"2942","Narrated 'Umar bin Al-Khattab:\I passed by Hisham bin Hakim bin Hizam while he was reciting Surat Al-Furqan during the lifetime of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). I listened to his recitation and noticed that he recited it in several different ways"""
"2943","Narrated Ubayy bin Ka'b:\The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) met Jibra'il and said: 'O Jibra'il! I have been sent to an illiterate nation among whom are the elderly woman"""
"2944","Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever alleviates a burden among the burdens of the world for his brother"""
"2945","Narrated 'Abdullah bin 'Amr :\I said: 'O Messenger of Allah! In how much time may I recite the Qur'an?' He said: 'Complete it in one month.' I said: 'I am able to do more than that.' He said: 'Then complete it in twenty (days).' I said: 'I am able to do more than that.' He said: 'Then finish it in fifteen (days).' I said: 'I am able to do more than that.' He said: 'Finish it in ten (days).' I said: 'I am able to do more than that.' He said: 'Finish it in five (days).' I said: 'I am able to do more than that.'\"" He ('Abdullah bin 'Amr) said: \""But he did not permit me"""
"2946","Narrated 'Abdullah bin 'Amr:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \Recite the Qur'an in forty (days)"""
"2947","Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:\A man said 'O Messenger of Allah! Which deed is most virtuous to Allah?' He said: 'Al-Hallul-Murtahil'' He said: 'What is Al-Hallul-Murtahil?' He said: 'The one who recites from the beginning of the Qur'an to the end of it"""
"2948","Narrated 'Abdullah bin 'Amr:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \He who recites the Qur'an in less than three (days)"""
"2949","Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever says (something) about the Qur'an without knowledge"""
